.TH HU_TERMINAL 3 "" "helios-unix" "Library functions"
.SH NAME
hu_terminal_size, hu_terminal_raw, hu_terminal_restore, hu_terminal_read, hu_set_nonblock \- use a native Helios terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <termios.h>
#include <helios/unix/api.h>

int hu_terminal_size(int fd, unsigned *rows, unsigned *columns);
int hu_terminal_raw(int fd, struct termios *saved);
int hu_terminal_restore(int fd, const struct termios *saved);
int hu_set_nonblock(int fd, int enabled);

struct hu_terminal_decoder {
    unsigned utf8_remaining;
    int helios_c1;
};
int hu_terminal_read(int fd, struct hu_terminal_decoder *decoder,
                     char *buffer, int size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
hu_terminal_size reads the current dimensions from native terminal attributes.
Query again after a resize notification. A SIGWINCH handler should set a flag;
read the dimensions in the application's normal control flow.
Helios uses attribute fields for dimensions which Unix uses for read timing;
do not overwrite these with Unix VMIN/VTIME settings.
.PP
hu_terminal_raw saves the full terminal state, then disables canonical input,
echo, terminal-generated signals, flow control and input/output translations.
Ctrl-C consequently arrives as input; the application must arrange its own
exit handling. Call hu_terminal_restore with the saved state on every exit
after successful raw-mode setup.
.PP
hu_set_nonblock changes O_NONBLOCK while preserving other descriptor flags.
This helper also works on non-terminal descriptors.
.SS Input profiles
Initialize a decoder once for each input stream. With helios_c1 set to 1,
hu_terminal_read expands standalone CSI (byte 0x9b) to ESC [ and SS3 (0x8f)
to ESC O. It preserves ordinary escape sequences and tracks UTF-8 continuation
bytes across reads so that those bytes are not expanded.
This is prefix conversion, not a complete function-key mapping or character
encoding conversion. Other terminal encodings need their own input policy.
.PP
The native Helios console converts recognised terminal keys into Helios key
sequences. The supplied xterm-ttyserv does the same: xterm sends ESC [ A for
Up, ttyserv maps it to 0x9b A, and an opted-in Unix application expands it
back to ESC [ A. Therefore TERM=xterm does not by itself mean that conversion
should be disabled. Select this profile according to the terminal service.
.PP
Set helios_c1 to 0 for an untranslated byte stream. Ordinary read calls are
never intercepted. Do not apply this terminal decoder to files or network
traffic. Keep the decoder state across calls; reset it when switching streams.
.PP
The output buffer must have at least two bytes. The result is not terminated
with a NUL. Reads can be short, and conversion can expand an input byte into
two output bytes.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Size, raw, restore and nonblock return 0 on success, or -1 with errno set.
hu_terminal_read returns the number of output bytes, 0 at end of input, or -1
with errno set. EAGAIN and EINTR retain their usual read meanings.
Invalid arguments or unavailable dimensions produce EINVAL.
.SH EXAMPLE
This routine prints one native key sequence as hexadecimal bytes and restores
the terminal. A full event loop must also arrange restoration on cancellation.
.EX
#include <termios.h>
#include <helios/unix/api.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <errno.h>

int show_key(void)
{
    struct termios saved;
    struct hu_terminal_decoder decoder = {0, 1};
    char bytes[32];
    int n, i, error;
    if (hu_terminal_raw(0, &saved) < 0) return -1;
    do {
        n = hu_terminal_read(0, &decoder, bytes, sizeof(bytes));
    } while (n < 0 && errno == EINTR);
    error = errno;
    if (hu_terminal_restore(0, &saved) < 0) return -1;
    if (n < 0) { errno = error; return -1; }
    for (i = 0; i < n; ++i)
        printf("%02x ", (unsigned char)bytes[i]);
    putchar('\en');
    return 0;
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
helios-unix(7), hu_poll(3)
